		(property "Note" "Q1 gate pull-down: holds the gate at 0V so Q1 is enhanced in normal polarity. Draws NO quiescent current - a MOSFET gate is capacitive, so current flows only while D3 is clamping. Worst case is D1 clamping at 38.9V: (38.9-15)/100k = 240 uA, i.e. 5.7 mW, well inside 0.1W. Value is not critical; 1% only for consistency with the other resistors."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
