		(property "Note" "EN slew limit: 470 pF with R17||R44 = 500k, tau ~0.24 ms, initial EN slope ~0.03 V/us (TPS7A16 limit 1.5 V/us). Kept small so D10's clamp current stays in the tens of uA. U9 EN circuit (review M1, 2026-10-12): EN = +12V/2 via R17/R44 (1M/1M), so EN <= IN by construction; Q4 holds EN at GND by default (gate biased from +12V by R45/R46), Q5 releases it when SENS_PWR_EN (GPIO19, J1 pin 35) is driven high. GPIO low, undriven or Pi off = sensor supply OFF; software turns it on (and can turn it off when parked). C32 sets the EN slew (< 1.5 V/us); D10 clamps EN to IN + ~0.2 V while +12V collapses faster than the 0.5 ms EN time constant. Replaces R17 330k from +3V3 + D10, whose hot leakage (up to 20 uA at 60 C) turned U9 on with the Pi off."
			(at 64.77 250.19 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
